{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"test:sub:cljs|test:sub\\\" bb.edn; rg -n \\\"defn.*dht-import|deftest|artifact|expected\\\" test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc | tail -20; sed -n '35,95p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md; rg -n \\\"compile|probe\\\" test/yang/python/antlr/e2e_test.clj test/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"394:  test:sub {:doc \"Subsystem tests, three lanes in parallel: bb test:sub <subsystem>... [--slow]\"\n404:  test:sub:clj {:doc \"JVM lane of test:sub: bb test:sub:clj <subsystem>... [--slow]\"\n414:  test:sub:cljs {:doc \"Node lane of test:sub: bb test:sub:cljs <subsystem>... [--slow]\"\n425:  test:sub:cljd {:doc \"Dart lane of test:sub: bb test:sub:cljd <subsystem>... [--slow]\"\n435:  test:sub:list {:doc \"What test:sub would run, prerequisites and seams: bb test:sub:list <subsystem>...\"\n839:  (let [artifact (fixture/read-file)\n840:        m (get-in artifact [:units \"m\"])\n842:        w (publish-world artifact)\n844:        src (hook-source artifact)\n846:              (run-over-dht w :semantic (get-in artifact [:importers :d]) src\n864:(defn- dht-import-test\n867:        _ (this-host-publishes-the-artifact lines)\n868:        artifact (fixture/read-file)\n869:        a (get-in artifact [:principals :a])\n871:        w (publish-world artifact)\n872:        w (hook-import-refused-without-the-index w artifact)\n873:        w (site-sets-over-the-mesh w artifact)\n874:        w (hook-import-with-the-index w artifact)\n875:        w (a-hook-import-chain w artifact)\n876:        w (imports-over-the-dht w artifact src)\n877:        w (an-untrusted-principal-is-refused-on-every-vm w artifact)\n878:        w (a-trusted-principal-is-allowed-on-every-vm w artifact)\n880:            w artifact)\n881:        w (republished-dependency-is-refused w artifact src)]\n887:(deftest ^:slow dht-import-test-test\n> (replaced by A; the `(R, H)` pairing becomes both being functions of\n> A). Invariant I is unchanged in substance; the linker contract\n> (`yin.vm.linker.md`) carries a coordinated amendment of the same date. The principle *\"one truth, many interpretations\"* quoted\n> in §1 **is not violated** (owner, 2026-10-10): the Universal AST is the\n> one truth and the three VMs remain its interpretations. Only §1's\n> narrower topology sentence, \"no projection is compiled from another\"\n> as applied at the de Bruijn layer, is superseded, since the register\n> image is now derived from A. R1's lowering walk changes input and is not a plug-in allocator over a\n> vector (Architect, `collab/yin-vm/1791510000000-architect-semantic-register-vm.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md`\n> finding 6).\n>\n> A second ruling of the same date makes the canonical semantic vector\n> register-shaped with virtual registers (*\"rebuilding the semantic-vm as\n> register shaped ... is the right way to go\"*); its design\n> (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`, forthcoming; landed and renamed\n> `yin.vm.semantic.md` at the 2026-10-15 cutover) will restate §4's\n> input and lowering contract. Not applied here.\n>\n> **Amendment 2026-10-15 (phase 8, 8g).** This kernel survived the\n> cutover: `debruijn/register.cljc` is a **backend** of the canonical\n> semantic kernel, executing the lowering `A → R` over the documented\n> fragment (continuation design §4.6), checked by the cross-engine laws\n> on that fragment. Refusal of the unsupported remainder before attach\n> remains the requirement; §4.6 lists the four implemented checks and the\n> harness-only exclusions, not a general fragment gate.\n> The old lowerers that produced its input are gone; `derive` lowers\n> from A. The fragment is not widened.\n\nThis document specifies a register execution path that is a peer of the\ncommitted de Bruijn stack path. Both are projections of the same de Bruijn\nencoding of the named semantic tuples; neither is derived from the other\n*(superseded 2026-10-10; see the amendment above)*.\nIt does not replace the named datoms, the stack image, the stack VM, or the\ndormant projection. The first deliverable is a pure resolved-tuples-to-\nregister lowerer and validator. The register VM kernel is a committed later\nphase, authorized by the owner without a benchmark condition (section 8,\nDECIDED 1).\n\n## 1. Objective and invariants\n\nThe objective is a deterministic register image derived from the de Bruijn\nencoding of the named `:yin/*` semantic tuples, at the same level as the\n`:yin.debruijn.code/*` stack image. The register lowerer consumes the\nresolved tuples and emits a register image; it never reads, rewrites, or\ndepends on the stack image. The stack image remains independently\naddressable by its existing H, and the register image is independently\naddressable by its own R.\n\nThis follows the project's established compilation topology\n(`docs/agents/architecture.md`, \"COMPILATION AS STREAM PROCESSING\"): one\nupstream stream feeds several parallel projections, and no projection is\ncompiled from another. That pattern is applied here one level down, at the\nde Bruijn layer.\n\nThis path is worth building on its own merits, and the merit is not\nperformance. The governing reason, in the owner's words, is that it\ndemonstrates the philosophy that one universal AST can be interpreted by\ndifferent VMs: one truth, many interpretations. The named datoms are this\nproject's single source of truth. The named VM, the stack VM, and the\nregister VM are not competing implementations with one canonical and the\nothers alternates; they are peer witnesses to the same truth, each free to\ntest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_test.clj:933:               #'programs/probe #'programs/admission #'programs/rebase\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:11:   stage answers the parser's packets, precompiled below (each def's\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:15:   The slow probe scenarios stay JVM-only.\"\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:30:    #?@(:cljd [] :clj [[yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as probe]])\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:38:;; Precompiled packets\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:122:   that answers the precompiled packets.\"\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:144:  \"The ids every session scenario runs under: the precompiled packets and\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:297:                   :lower #(yang.clojure/compile (first %)),\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:299:                                    [(yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:406:;; The parser and the probe (JVM)\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:414:(deftest precompiled-packets-are-the-parsers-test\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:427:   (deftest ^:slow probe-buffers-an-open-block-test\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:445:   (deftest ^:slow probe-buffers-across-lines-test\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:468:   (deftest ^:slow probed-lines-keep-their-whitespace-test\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:474:       (is (= :complete (probe/probe \"s = 'a\\\\  \")))\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:484:   (deftest ^:slow probe-reports-irreparable-errors-at-once-test\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:491:         (is (= :complete (probe/probe bad)))\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:502:   (deftest probe-classifies-test\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:533:       (is (= expected (probe/probe text)) (pr-str text)))))\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:545:(deftest compile-previews-the-submitted-form-not-the-prelude-test\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:549:            [after text] (repl/eval-input fresh \"(compile \\\"1 + 2\\\")\")]\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:558:(deftest compile-error-path-test\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:560:                                  \"(compile 1)\")]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
