-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| S6     | Heap and portability: collection, pinning, scalar UCF round trips,  |\n|        | cell-lift and raw-transport refusals, version-0 refusal. Landed.    |\n+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| S7     | Integration gate over the full C1 and C3 corpus, profile mismatch,  |\n|        | and resource-limit fixtures: corpus `c3-corpus-v1`, `admit`,        |\n|        | `data/max-items`, the `round` argument order. Landed.               |\n+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\nC3 is complete only with (ruling 14):\n\n- All four VMs on JVM, Node, and Dart VM, twelve lanes; Dart compiled to\n  JavaScript is not claimed. Source-level tests run on the JVM and\n  parserless forms on Node and Dart.\n- Golden byte fixtures checked on each host, in place of directed\n  host-pair runs, and unchanged Jing fixtures.\n- The full C1 corpus.\n- Generated operands from a checked-in table with CPython-computed\n  expectations, not a host RNG. The corpus covers the boundaries around\n  2^53, 2^63, and 2^64, promotion followed by cancellation, the\n  `divmod`, shift, power, conversion, key, and `hash(-1)` detectors, and\n  the C1 signed-zero cases.\n- Mutation evidence, each mutation shown failing its detector once and\n  recorded in the engineer's report: disabled promotion, skipped\n  demotion, double-coerced keys, omitted floor adjustment, `abs(n)` for\n  tag 3, host `number?` as the only scalar gate, and a prematurely\n  narrowed shift count.\n\nThe detectors are source programs (S7): `c3_programs.cljc` holds ten,\none per theme (promotion, demotion, keys, divmod, shifts, power,\ndocs/design/yin-repl-design.md:175:(`:semantic`, `:register`, `:stack`, `:space`) were deleted under\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1:# yin.vm.semantic: the canonical projection rebuilt register-shaped\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:5:`collab/yin-vm/1791510000000-architect-semantic-register-vm.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:10:`semantic-register-vm` (this file was\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:11:`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`); the phase-8 cutover (2026-10-15)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:75:> \"rebuilding the semantic-vm as as register shaped instead of\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:78:> with virtual registers. once we build semantic-register-vm we can\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:79:> delete semantic-vm and rename semantic-register-vm to sematic-vm\")\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1038:semantic registers and frames (§5.1) and identity sections; the row\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1100:4. **Evaluator.** `yin.vm.semantic-register` beside `yin.vm.semantic`.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1102:   `:yin.semantic-register/code`, contract `\"v4\"`; phase 5 supplies its\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1159:   frames** (the semantic kernel, the stack and register kernels through\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1183:   `yin.vm.semantic-register` to `yin.vm.semantic`, remove the old H/R\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
