{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '135,190p' docs/design/yin-repl-design.md; rg -n \\\"8\\\\.5\\\\.6|vm\\\" docs/design/yang.antlr.md | tail -15\"","aggregated_output":"- `:php` → `yang.php/compile`\n\n### `handle-command [state form]` → `[new-state print-msg]`\n\nDispatch shell commands:\n\n| Command | Effect |\n|---------|--------|\n| `(vm :ast-walker)` | Reset to a fresh ASTWalkerVM (warns about lost store) |\n| `(lang :python)` | Switch input language to Python (no VM change) |\n| `(compile expr)` | Compile expression to AST + datoms; print them; do NOT execute |\n| `(reset)` | Create fresh VM of same type |\n| `(connect \"daostream:ws://host:port\")` | Connect to remote shell; forward evals |\n| `(disconnect)` | Close remote connection; resume local eval |\n| `(telemetry)` | Toggle telemetry to stderr |\n| `(telemetry \"daostream:ws://host:port\")` | Stream telemetry to remote WebSocket |\n| `(help)` | Print help text |\n| `(quit)` | Exit shell |\n\n### `make-vm [vm-type telemetry-stream]` → `<vm>`\n\nCreate a fresh VM instance. If `telemetry-stream` is non-nil, wire the VM to emit `[e a v t m]` datoms to that stream on every step, park, resume, halt, and effect.\n\n### `enable-telemetry! [state-atom sink]`\n\nStart telemetry streaming.\n- `sink = :stderr` — background loop reads datoms from telemetry stream, pretty-prints to stderr\n- `sink = \"daostream:ws://...\"` — relay datoms to remote WebSocket\n\n### `serve! [state-atom port]`\n\nExpose the shell as a WebSocket server. Accept remote clients and dispatch `:op/eval`, `:op/vm`, `:op/lang`, `:op/reset` requests via `dao.stream.apply` protocol.\n\n---\n\n## Shell Commands\n\n### `(vm :ast-walker)`\n\n`:ast-walker` is the only supported VM backend; the others\n(`:semantic`, `:register`, `:stack`, `:space`) were deleted under\n`yin.vm-consumers.implementation-plan.md`. Warns that `:store` state is\nlost and creates a fresh VM.\n\n```clojure\nyin> (vm :ast-walker)\nSwitched to ASTWalkerVM (store cleared)\nyin> (def x 10)\nnil\nyin> x\n10\n```\n\n### `(lang :clojure | :python | :php)`\n\nSwitch the input language for source code compilation. Does not affect the current VM.\n2639:is `checked-divide`), `= == !=` stay host `=`, and nothing in `yin.vm`\n2720:gates in `yin.vm` and `yin.vm.engine`. If C3-S2 edits those gates, the\n2723:#### 8.5.6 Imports, the linked prelude, and the frontend catalog (phase C4)\n3060:  staged stage load (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 4.1 step 5). Known gaps: SCC\n3171:(`yin.vm.linker.dht.md` section 7.5, slices AL-1 to AL-4), which is\n3236:| I3    | Publication and DHT import; admission per `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 7.5 |\n3344:  moves the name meanwhile (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 7.5, AD-2). Landed in\n3364:  (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md` section 7.5). The\n3375:  `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` section 7.5 (slices AL-1 to AL-4). Also:\n3381:  that closes this lands with L-d (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 7.4).\n3953:as section 8.5.6 requires. Install children must not export live function\n3959:stay beside code under `yin.vm.typecheck`, not in lambda language tags.\n4379:runtime profile, not in the standard `vm/primitives` registry, whose\n4381:decision 3). The module is `yin.vm.data`, module name `data`, landed in\n4405:grammar of `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` section 2.3 has no class, method,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
